package com.hereliesaz.hg2gui.terminal

/**
 * Maps every executable/shared-library file the bundled Termux bootstrap needs to run to the
 * flattened, exec-exempt copy of it shipped as a native lib - `composeApp/src/main/jniLibs/
 * arm64-v8a/`, generated by renaming each real bootstrap path (e.g. `bin/bash`) into an
 * Android-legal `lib<mangled-path>.so` filename (e.g. `libbin_bash.so`).
 *
 * Android's write-xor-execute policy (enforced on every device this app targets, API 29+) blocks
 * executing a binary extracted into ordinary app-private storage (`context.filesDir`) - only a
 * file the OS itself installed as a native lib, into `context.applicationInfo.nativeLibraryDir`,
 * is exempt. A downloaded Termux bootstrap's own `bin/bash`, `lib/libc++_shared.so`, etc. can
 * never qualify for that exemption no matter when or how they're extracted; only files that
 * shipped inside the APK itself, in `jniLibs/`, do. This is the same trick already used for the
 * bundled `libzsh.so` (see [ShellSession.forAndroid]), extended to the whole bootstrap.
 *
 * [DistroManager] uses this to symlink every one of these real paths, under the downloaded
 * bootstrap's own `$PREFIX`, to its bundled counterpart in `nativeLibraryDir` - so `$PREFIX/bin/
 * bash` (and everything it in turn execs or dynamically links against) resolves to a file the OS
 * will actually run, while every other file in the bootstrap (configs, docs, dpkg's own package
 * database, Python/Perl scripts, ...) still comes from the ordinary download, since only
 * *executing* a file needs this - reading one doesn't.
 *
 * Regenerating this file (a new Termux bootstrap release, a different set of packages) means
 * re-running the same flatten step against the new bootstrap-aarch64.zip: for every file whose
 * first four bytes are the ELF magic number under bin/, lib/, or libexec/ (skipping libexec/
 * installed-tests/, which is bootstrap-internal test tooling, not something a shell session ever
 * runs), flatten(path) = "lib" + path.replace(anything not [a-zA-Z0-9_-], "_") + ".so", copy the
 * real file to that name under jniLibs/arm64-v8a/, and regenerate this table from the result.
 */
object BootstrapManifest {
